cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "terrastat: public time series from the world's statistical agencies, with provenance attached"
message: >-
  If you use this software or a corpus built with it, please cite it.
  The data itself carries separate attribution requirements from the
  statistical agencies that published it — see ATTRIBUTIONS.md in any
  snapshot, and the per-series `attribution` column.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Montero-Manso
    given-names: Pablo
    affiliation: University of Sydney
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"   # fill in
repository-code: "https://github.com/pmontman/terrastat"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-08"
keywords:
  - time series
  - forecasting
  - economic data
  - FRED
  - Eurostat
  - OECD
  - dataset
abstract: >-
  terrastat gathers public economic time series from FRED, Eurostat and the
  OECD into a tidy, licence-aware Parquet database. Every series resolves to
  one uniform 36-column schema carrying its own licence, attribution text and
  provenance, so a redistributable subset can be selected and published with
  the citations each source requires. It includes tools for assessing the
  corpus — length, recency, information content, aggregation hierarchies —
  and for the leakage that arises when three sources republish one another.
